```apex
public class HouseholdService {

    /**
     * Creates a single NPSP Household Account and inserts the supplied (new) contacts
     * into it. The first contact in the list becomes the household's primary contact.
     *
     * @param members  A non-null, non-empty list of new Contact records (no Id, no AccountId).
     * @return         The Id of the newly created Household Account.
     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if members is null or empty, or the Household
     *                                  RecordType is not found.
     */
    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not be null or empty');
        }

        // Dynamically resolve the Household RecordType – no hard-coded Ids
        RecordType householdRT = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM RecordType
            WHERE SobjectType = 'Account'
              AND Name = 'Household'
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        if (householdRT == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('Household RecordType not found on Account');
        }

        // Savepoint so that no empty/extra household is left behind if any DML fails
        Savepoint sp = Database.setSavepoint();

        Account household;
        try {
            // Create ONE NPSP household account.
            // We intentionally do NOT set Account.Name – NPSP's naming trigger
            // will generate the household name and greetings automatically.
            household = new Account(
                RecordTypeId = householdRT.Id
            );
            insert household;

            // Link every contact to the new household
            for (Contact c : members) {
                c.AccountId = household.Id;
            }
            insert members;

            // Designate the first contact in the list as the primary contact
            household.Primary_Contact__c = members[0].Id;
            update household;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Database.rollback(sp);
            throw e;
        }

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **NPSP household identification** | The `RecordTypeId` is resolved at runtime by querying `RecordType` for `SobjectType = 'Account'` and `Name = 'Household'`. No hard-coded Ids. |
| **No name set by us** | `Account.Name` is never assigned, so NPSP's household-naming trigger (which keys off the Household RecordType) computes the name and generates the greeting fields. |
| **Exactly one account** | A single `insert` of one `Account` is the only DML that creates an account. All contacts receive that same `AccountId` before their own insert, so no orphan contacts can trigger additional household creation. |
| **No leftover on failure** | A `Savepoint` is set before any DML. If any subsequent insert/update throws, the savepoint is rolled back, guaranteeing no empty household remains. |
| **Primary contact** | After all contacts are inserted (so the lookup target exists), the first contact's Id is written to `Account.Primary_Contact__c` and the account is updated. |
| **Bulk-safe** | One SOQL (RecordType lookup), three DML statements, no per-record SOQL in a loop – safe for up to 200 contacts. |

